-- title:
--   Nonnegativity of the Huber function
-- statement:
--   For every $c \ge 0$ the Huber function is nonnegative everywhere:
--
--   $$H_c(t) \ge 0 \qquad \text{for all } t \in \mathbb{R}, \qquad H_c(t) = \begin{cases} t^2/2, & |t| \le c,\\[2pt] c|t| - c^2/2, & |t| \ge c.\end{cases}$$
--
--   On the quadratic branch the value is the square $t^2/2 = |t|^2/2 \ge 0$; on the linear branch $|t| \ge c$ together with $c \ge 0$ gives $c|t| \ge c^2$, whence $c|t| - c^2/2 \ge c^2/2 \ge 0$. The two branches agree at $|t| = c$, so no gap arises at the junction.
-- source:
--   《有理动量 Nesterov 紧界与半径归一化五算法共同最坏情形 — 可审计完整证明稿》 (manuscript, 2026-10-08), §25, eq. (25.2); Lean: FullFormalization.LiftedHuber lines 109-116

